#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:5
#: fb40eb548e89406693138f1c15a55319
msgid "Circle Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:7
#: 5f66acd624c54c36aeeafeae84b8c000
msgid "Circle will orbit a point located :ref:`CIRCLE_RADIUS_M<CIRCLE_RADIUS_M>` centimeters in front of the vehicle with the nose of the vehicle pointed at the center."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:12
#: f2f60185d4644b9b8f9d183bb945419d
msgid "The units are **meters**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:14
#: e753a74a7f9d4603982c55b8002d644d
msgid "Setting the :ref:`CIRCLE_RADIUS_M<CIRCLE_RADIUS_M>` to zero will cause the copter to simply stay in place and slowly rotate (useful for panorama shots)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:17
#: f8726a8e649945ffa9506228da895ad0
msgid "The speed of the vehicle (in deg/second) can be modified by changing the :ref:`CIRCLE_RATE<CIRCLE_RATE>` parameter.  A positive value means rotate clockwise, a negative means counter clockwise.  The vehicle may not achieve the desired rate if this requires the acceleration towards the center of the circle to exceed about half of the maximum acceleration held in the :ref:`WP_ACC<WP_ACC>` parameter (units are m/s/s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:24
#: 21d1f16ceb834c9fa69c33f48fb61acb
msgid "The circle rate set above can be dynamically adjusted in flight by two methods. The first is the use of RC Channel 6 if the :ref:`TUNE<TUNE>` option is set to 39, with the minimum and maximum circle rates set by :ref:`TUNE_MIN<TUNE_MIN>` and :ref:`TUNE_MAX<TUNE_MAX>`. The other is by enabling bit 0 of the :ref:`CIRCLE_OPTIONS<CIRCLE_OPTIONS>` bitmask parameter to allow stick adjustment of radius and speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:27
#: 94dd84f7cccd4d3a9a161eb2e4901af0
msgid "Circle Control Option"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:29
#: 436a5c1e146c46d6b0b1c2b199101fe0
msgid "The :ref:`CIRCLE_OPTIONS<CIRCLE_OPTIONS>` bitmask parameter controls what actions the pilot can adjust with his sticks and circle mode operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:31
#: 6ff291d1e1ec47a9bdceec8af0166d15
msgid "When bit 0 is set of the :ref:`CIRCLE_OPTIONS<CIRCLE_OPTIONS>` parameter the pilot can adjust circle's radius and angular velocity with the control sticks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:33
#: d47c4969fd1a4911b9ecf3dc72335ea6
msgid "Pitch stick up (reducing RC pwm) reduces the radius until it reaches zero. Think moving forward from an FPV perspective."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:34
#: 1c14f6e12b5c4efe87b5249ceb363af0
msgid "Pitch stick down (increasing RC pwm) increases the radius. Think moving back from an FPV perspective."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:35
#: d768209d959c4a74bd3d051028f9d1a9
msgid "Roll stick right (think clockwise) will increase the speed while moving clockwise, or decrease the speed while moving counterclockwise until reaching zero, at which point it will stop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:36
#: a8977dd47ac34724bbc5cfbf8630d3ee
msgid "Roll stick left (think counterclockwise) will increase the speed while moving counterclockwise, or decrease the speed while moving clockwise until reaching zero, at which point it will stop. Once stopped (rate 0), releasing the roll stick and pushing it again in either direction will begin moving again in the desired direction. So yes, this allows you to completely change the direction on the fly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:37
#: cb9f17147a644b8c8d0d4e709a7b2614
msgid "Roll stick rate changes are inhibited when CH6 tuning knob is set for circle rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:38
#: 8f7cdfa451274284af32603d7d37d8d2
msgid "All stick changes are inhibited in radio failsafe.(ie if loiter turns was part of a mission that continues when in failsafe)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:39
#: e2549f520a9b4dcd9c82ee5fdfb5f4f0
msgid "The above does not actually change the stored circle_rate or circle_radius parameter. Upon rebooting, any stick changes to rate and radius are gone and it will use the parameter values. So users should not have any surprises with every new flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:41
#: 244f1f01e12f40099b8f001367942206
msgid "When bit 1 is set of the :ref:`CIRCLE_OPTIONS<CIRCLE_OPTIONS>` parameter the Copter will face the direction of travel as it circles, otherwise, the Copter will point its nose at the center of the circle as it orbits. When bit 2 is set of the :ref:`CIRCLE_OPTIONS<CIRCLE_OPTIONS>` parameter the circle's center position will set upon mode entry at the current location, rather than on the perimeter with the center in front of the Copter at the start. When bit 3 is set of the :ref:`CIRCLE_OPTIONS<CIRCLE_OPTIONS>` parameter the mount's (if used) ROI aka region of interest will be set on the circle center causing mount to face the circle's center all the times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:46
#: 0f83b6c58297487c956f69691b21822d
msgid "Other Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:48
#: e0236568a59c46d18a89f57e00d0e7a2
msgid "When :ref:`CIRCLE_OPTIONS<CIRCLE_OPTIONS>` bit 0 is not set, the pilot does not have any control over the roll and pitch but can change the altitude with the throttle stick as in :ref:`altholdmode` or :ref:`loiter-mode`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:50
#: 198e3fffec0645fbbb836cdc83be12cb
msgid "The pilot can control the yaw of the copter, but the autopilot will not retake control of the yaw until circle mode is re-engaged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:52
#: 3358745536e7485c9db5449c23ef6520
msgid "If the Rover cannot maintain a track close the  circle desired it will automatically decrease speed until it can maintain the desired track."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:54
#: d4483e75374d4b2ab550473c6318d07e
msgid "The mission command ``LOITER_TURNS`` invokes Circle mode during a mission."
msgstr ""
